        "article_text_excerpt": "“Acting on my instructions, on Tuesday the relevant official from the Ministry of Foreign Affairs informed the Russian ambassador to Hungary that, according to the assessment of the Hungarian authorities, 10 members of the Russian mission had engaged in activities in Hungary that are unacceptable for diplomats under the Vienna Convention. The Hungarian side has therefore called on the individuals in question to leave Hungary. This decision protects Hungary’s security and sovereignty”-- Hungarian Foreign Minister Anita Orbán announced on her Facebook page. An expulsion of this magnitude is unprecedented; never before have so many Russian diplomats been sent home from the country. The Minister added that the move “does not imply breaking off diplomatic relations with Russia. Hungary intends to continue the necessary dialogue, based on mutual respect and adherence to the rules.” The Russian Ministry of Foreign Affairs responded to the news by saying: Russia will respond to the expulsion o",
